---
const description =
  "I'll run an automated private job search customized just for you.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#FFFFFF" />
    <title>Job Fiend — doodle try</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Delius+Swash+Caps&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --primary: #49b6e5;
        --secondary: #263d5b;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --text: #111827;
        --space-2: 0.5rem;
        --space-3: 0.75rem;
        --space-4: 1rem;
        --space-6: 1.5rem;
        --space-8: 2rem;
        --space-12: 3rem;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }

      html { background: var(--surface); }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--text);
        background: var(--surface);
        font-family: 'Delius Swash Caps', 'Segoe Script', cursive;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      ::selection {
        background: var(--primary);
        color: var(--surface);
      }

      .sketch {
        position: absolute;
        width: 0;
        height: 0;
      }

      .page {
        width: min(40rem, calc(100% - 2.5rem));
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: var(--space-12) 0 5rem;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
        font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 10vw, 4rem);
        font-weight: 400;
        line-height: 1.05;
      }

      .scribble {
        display: block;
        width: min(14rem, 70%);
        height: 18px;
        margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
      }

      .lede {
        margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
        font-size: 1.45rem;
        line-height: 1.45;
      }

      .actions {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
        align-items: center;
        margin: 0 0 var(--space-12);
      }

      .book {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        min-height: 48px;
        padding: 0.55rem 1.15rem;
        color: var(--surface);
        background: var(--secondary);
        text-decoration: none;
        filter: url(#wobble);
      }

      .book:hover { background: #1b2d44; }
      .book:focus-visible {
        outline: 3px solid var(--primary);
        outline-offset: 4px;
      }

      .repo {
        color: var(--secondary);
        text-underline-offset: 0.28em;
      }

      .copy p {
        margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
      }

      .copy p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

      .arrow {
        display: block;
        width: 4.5rem;
        height: 3rem;
        margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-3);
      }

      .demo {
        margin-top: var(--space-12);
      }

      .demo-frame {
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
        aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
        background: #f3f6f9;
        filter: url(#wobble);
      }

      .demo-frame iframe {
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        border: 0;
      }

      .note {
        margin: var(--space-8) 0 0;
        font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        color: var(--secondary);
      }

      .note a { color: inherit; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <svg class="sketch" aria-hidden="true">
      <filter id="wobble" x="-8%" y="-8%" width="116%" height="116%">
        <feTurbulence type="fractalNoise" baseFrequency="0.04" numOctaves="2" seed="3" result="n" />
        <feDisplacementMap in="SourceGraphic" in2="n" scale="2.4" />
      </filter>
    </svg>
    <main class="page">
      <h1>Job Fiend</h1>
      <svg class="scribble" viewBox="0 0 220 18" aria-hidden="true">
        <path
          d="M2 11 C 28 4, 46 16, 72 9 S 120 17, 148 8 S 196 15, 218 10"
          fill="none"
          stroke="#49B6E5"
          stroke-width="3"
          stroke-linecap="round"
        />
      </svg>
      <p class="lede">{description}</p>
      <svg class="arrow" viewBox="0 0 72 48" aria-hidden="true">
        <path
          d="M6 8 C 18 28, 34 34, 58 22"
          fill="none"
          stroke="#263D5B"
          stroke-width="2.4"
          stroke-linecap="round"
        />
        <path
          d="M46 14 L 60 22 L 44 30"
          fill="none"
          stroke="#263D5B"
          stroke-width="2.4"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
        />
      </svg>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="book" href="https://cal.com/alexlazar/30-min-meeting">Book a setup</a>
        <a
          class="repo"
          href="https://github.com/mauricedesaxe/job-finder"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Github Repo</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          My system will search for jobs for you every day based on criteria you
          provided and then put them in a review queue. As you pursue or reject
          provided jobs, the system learns what you want and gives you more of that.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything is open source and the system itself, not including its various
          underlying vendors and providers, is free to use. This means that you can
          set it up yourself but to abstract that work from you, I offer a limited
          number of free managed plans.
        </p>
        <p>
          We book a call and I spend time with you learning about you. I want to
          know about your experiences. I want to know about your needs, wants, and
          desires. We point the system at your profile while on the call and we look
          at the first few jobs it finds together.
        </p>
        <p>
          Once we're done with our call, the system should have some degree of
          understanding about what jobs you want and it should give you more jobs
          every day. I want you to review them. I want you to give feedback when a
          job is bad and when a job is good and why.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is the core value exchange I'm asking for from you. My system will
          absolutely find you jobs once it's past that initial learning phase. I
          know because it found me jobs that I liked and applied to. But I need to
          be able to collect this feedback from you to be able to improve the system
          even further so that more people can benefit from it.
        </p>
        <p>
          As everything stands right now I'm not making any money from this. I'm not
          charging you. I'm not charging the employer. In fact I'm spending out of
          pocket on all the vendors and providers underneath the system that will
          run for you. I do this, of course, not out of the kindness of my soul. I
          am hoping that as I show this to more people and I gather more feedback, I
          will eventually be able to turn it into some sort of a commercial project.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-frame">
          <iframe
            src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/bO7vzA0xbWg"
            title="Job Fiend demo"
            allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
            allowfullscreen
            loading="lazy"></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note"><a href="/">Live poster version</a></p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
